{"subject": "maths", "level": "ibdp", "topic_display": "Statistics: Distributions (HL)", "topic_slug": "statistics--distributions-hl", "theme": "maths-grid", "adventure_n": 3, "title": "t-distribution, Chi-square and Regression", "emoji": "📉", "welcome_lead": "Test hypotheses and fit lines: t, chi-square and linear regression in action.", "meta_desc": "HL Maths adventure on t-distribution, chi-square test and linear regression.", "final_note": "t for small samples, chi-square for categorical, regression for trends!", "concepts": [{"term": "t-distribution", "def": "Bell shape with heavier tails; df = n - 1."}, {"term": "Chi-square stat", "def": "χ^2 = Σ (O - E)^2 / E across categories."}, {"term": "Degrees of freedom", "def": "Independent pieces of information."}, {"term": "Linear regression", "def": "y = a + bx, line of best fit via least squares."}, {"term": "Pearson r", "def": "Correlation in [-1, 1] for linear strength."}, {"term": "Null hypothesis", "def": "H_0: no association or no difference."}], "walkthroughs": [{"tag": "tt", "h2": "t-test Statistic", "body_html": "<p>Sample mean 52, μ_0 = 50, s = 4, n = 16.</p><p>t = (52-50)/(4/√16) = 2/1 = 2 with 15 df.</p>"}, {"tag": "chi", "h2": "Chi-square Test", "body_html": "<p>Observed 20, 30; Expected 25, 25.</p><p>χ^2 = (20-25)^2/25 + (30-25)^2/25 = 1 + 1 = 2.</p>"}, {"tag": "reg", "h2": "Regression Slope", "body_html": "<p>For 5 pairs, Σx=15, Σy=20, Σxy=80, Σx^2=55.</p><p>b = (5(80) - 15(20))/(5(55)-225) = (400-300)/50 = 2.</p>"}], "mcqs": [{"q": "Chi-square statistic uses:", "options": [["Σ (O - E)^2 / E", 1], ["Σ (O - E)^2", 0], ["Σ |O - E|", 0], ["O × E", 0]]}, {"q": "t-distribution is used when:", "options": [["sample is small, σ unknown", 1], ["population known and infinite", 0], ["categorical only", 0], ["proportions only", 0]]}], "numericals": [{"q": "df for one-sample t-test, n = 20?", "options": [18, 19, 20, 21], "answer": 19}], "free_texts": [{"q": "Correlation coefficient symbol (letter)?", "answer": "r"}]}